message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the work below."
title: "What Improves Akkadian Machine Translation, and What Only Seems To?"
abstract: >-
  A study of what improves machine translation for Old Assyrian Akkadian and
  what only seems to. Under one shared fine-tuning recipe, byte-level models
  lead subword models by a wide margin and every preprocessing intervention
  hurts the larger model. Choosing the learning rate per configuration removes
  most of both effects. Data quantity and model size are the two choices with
  reliable effects.
